                <pb facs="0700" n="600" sameAs="frus:frus1934v01/pg600"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.515 Gold Bloc/4: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul at Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-10-05T19:00:00-05:00">October 5, 1934—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>100. Your 287, October 3rd. Please inform Stoppani that this Government is
                    distinctly interested in the work of the Joint Committee and wishes to
                    participate.</p>
                <p>Will communicate with you again next week in regard to the three alternative
                    methods of participation which are suggested in your cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
